File: /Volumes/Attic/Desktop/Projects/crates/oscore/src/edhoc/kdf.rs
Lines: 91-101

edhoc_kdf creates okm, expands into it, then copies to result:
```rust
let mut okm = heapless::Vec::<u8, 128>::new();
okm.resize(length, 0).map_err(...)?;
hk.expand(&info, &mut okm).map_err(...)?;
let mut result = heapless::Vec::new();
result.extend_from_slice(okm.as_slice()).map_err(...)?;
Ok(result)
```

This copy serves no purpose (both are heapless::Vec<u8, 128>) and is worse for security: it leaves key material in TWO stack locations (okm and result), neither of which is zeroized on drop.

Fix: Return okm directly: `Ok(okm)`
